### Admission (I3 §1.2)
All of: licence CC0/CC BY/CC BY-SA or US public domain; no NC/ND; no third-party-held content (manual judgment); PD basis explicit (before 1931, no/defective notice, not renewed; underlying work also PD); a fixed master with checksum. Trailers/extras never candidates.
### Annotations (I3 §1.3)
Shots (frame+time of each cut, automatic); dialogue (start/end/text, ASR); description 1-3 sentences "[景别] 的 [主体] [动作]，[运镜]", characters C1, C2..., no colour/lens/style, VLM-drafted; hierarchy L0-L4; provenance fingerprints (frame+audio) from master. Human corrections out of scope.
### Hierarchy and tasks (I3 §1.4; CFG benchmark.yaml)
- L0 shot. L1 beat: 2-8 consecutive shots in one scene, <=40 s; over-40 s shot or lone shot is its own beat (CFG min_shots 2, max_shots 8, max_seconds 40).
- L2 scene: boundary where the 3 shots before and after are mutually dissimilar by shot-appearance similarity; scenes <12 s merge into the previous (CFG link_window_shots 3, kappa 1.0 [CFG only], min_seconds 12).
- L3: 2-6 scenes, <=10 min; over-long single scene alone (CFG max_scenes 6, max_seconds 600). L4: whole film, only films <=15 min (CFG max_seconds 900) - so Sherlock Jr. (44.1 min) has no L4.
- Sampling: L0 30 shots, L1 15 beats per film, duration-stratified, seed set by the film; fewer -> all (CFG sample_per_film).
- Tasks: every L2/L3/L4 segment plus sampled L0/L1; tracks Reference (`ref`) and Screenplay (`scr`). Dev totals (6 films): L0 155 segs/310 tasks, L1 69/138, L2 56/112, L3 14/28, L4 5/10; 299 segments, 598 tasks (I3 §1.4). Per-film task counts are not in I3 (Caminandes 3: 90, I3 §1.6; Coffee Run: 28 per OBJ).
- Task contents: instructions, delivery spec, tier tool list, budget per minute of segment: model $20, tools $5, 1 h wall clock, floor 15 min (CFG wall_clock_floor_minutes 15), input (Reference: original segment; Screenplay: script of dialogue+times and shot table of times+descriptions), answer used only for scoring, never visible.
### Systems and run rules (I3 §2.1-2.3; CFG)
- Fixed pipeline: no agent, no feedback loop; one still + slow push per shot, one synthetic voice per speaker, one background music, cut at the cut points; leaderboard floor. Single agents and crews as in OBJ; crew = 1 director + 6 roles; same base model, tools, budget.
- Isolation; no answer visible; all model calls metered through the billing proxy and refused once the model budget is spent; all generator calls through one tool server at fixed prices, refusing original inputs; uniform event log (model calls, tool calls, file writes, inter-role messages, each delivered version).
- Tiers: T0 image generate/edit, speech, music, sfx, video edit (CFG: image.generate, image.edit, speech.synthesize, music.generate, sfx.generate, media.ffmpeg); T1 = T0 + video generation, Wan 2.2 (CFG: video.generate, Wan-AI/Wan2.2-T2V-A14B-Diffusers and I2V-A14B-Diffusers, 1280x720, self-hosted per CFG vs Alibaba-hosted per OBJ - G11); T2 own generators, ranked separately (not this stage). CFG profile `smoke` replaces all generators with placeholders, runs unofficial (G1).
- Delivery: MP4 H.264, 1280x720, 24 fps (CFG yuv420p); AAC stereo 48 kHz; English WebVTT; manifest of assets; duration within +-5% of the segment.
- Runs per task: I3 §2.4 says 3 (L4: 2) (CFG runs default 3, L4 2); OBJ asks 1 per system per task this stage (G4).
### Scoring (I3 §2.4)
R = (Q, Q.c, Q.S, $). Q pass/fail: decodes fully with picture and sound; format per spec; duration +-5%; subtitles cover every dialogue line; log shows no generator read original input; provenance finds no original frame/audio. Q fail => c, S zero.
c: cut F1 at 0.5 s and 1.0 s; shot correspondence (judge sees only the original shot description and the remake's same period at 1 frame/s, 2-8 frames; duration-weighted); dialogue WER and onset-time error; speaker/character consistency (cluster purity); scene order. Judge must be a different vendor from the system's base model. S: out of scope this stage.
$: total cost, cost per minute of remade film, time per minute, call count, delivered versions, share of unused generated assets, cost by role, cost-quality Pareto frontier (I3 §2.4).
Provenance thresholds (CFG only; I3 §2.5 sets them on the stress test, out of scope): frame_sample_fps 2, phash_max_hamming 10, dino_min_cosine 0.92, audio_min_match 0.35, max_false_flag_rate 0.01. Continuity (CFG): cut_tolerance_s [0.5, 1.0], judge frames/s 1, min 2, max 8.
### Release / evidence (I3 §1.5, §2.6)
Master verified by checksum; annotations, descriptions with model recorded, fingerprints, task packages; agreement evidence with dataset `d509bed` (cuts, dialogue, hierarchy, task list), every difference listed and explained; README states verified status. Dev: every system runs on dev tasks and gets a full R (I3 §2.6).
### Prices
CFG `prices.yaml`: only a `default` token price (input 5.00, output 25.00, cache_read 0.50, cache_write 6.25 USD/M tokens), model-specific rows are empty placeholders; CFG `tools.yaml` lists illustrative tool prices (image 0.04/call, speech 0.015/1k chars, music and sfx 0.002/s, video 0.0008/GPU-s). Both are old-implementation values, not protocol; the price table for this stage is task-maker's from official pages (OBJ req 2); see G12.

